The api class has 4 functions you need to know about

----------------------------------------------------------------
@app.route('/syllabi', methods=['GET']) needs no input you call this and get a list of the syllabi
including size, id and name
----------------------------------------------------------------
@app.route('/syllabus/<int:syllabus_id>', methods=['GET']) query for 1 pdf, returns json data. NEEDS id of pdf
as argument
----------------------------------------------------------------
@app.route('/uploadPdf', methods=['POST'])
to give an example of how to implement this
<form action="/uploadPdf" method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data">
        <label for="fileInput">Choose PDF File:</label><br><br>
        <input type="file" id="fileInput" name="file" accept=".pdf" required>
        <br><br>
        <input type="submit" value="Upload PDF">
</form>
as you can see all you need to do is provide the id and name and my db manager will store it as a byte string
----------------------------------------------------------------
@app.route('/displayPDF/<pdfName>', methods=['GET'])
this actually returns the pdf file as a byte string buffer
all you need to pass as an argument is the pdfname
an example of how to implement
<iframe
        src="/displayPDF/{{ pdf_filename }}"
        class="pdf-viewer"
        title="Embedded PDF Document">
 </iframe>
